## 1. Context
- My app is a Spotify-like music app: **Android, Kotlin, Jetpack Compose** (Material 3). Repo: https://github.com/alaktracare-sys/studiopp.git
- `MainShell.kt` holds the floating bottom navigation (Home, Search, Library, Pins).
- **Do not change** the existing player, queue, shuffle or loop logic. Only add the feature below and the small hooks it needs.

## 2. What to build
A "Your Sound Capsule" feature made of **4 screens**, plus the listening tracking that feeds them.

### Screen 1 – Your Sound Capsule (home)
- Top bar: back arrow on the left, title "Your Sound Capsule" centered (16 sp, ExtraBold, white).
- Month row: month + year ("October 2026", 20 sp, ExtraBold) with an info icon. Tapping the month opens a dropdown to pick another month (last 12 months).
- Card **Time listened**: label "Time listened", below it the big number in green, e.g. "1,248 minutes" (32 sp, ExtraBold). **Tapping it opens Screen 4.**
- Two cards side by side (equal width):
  - **Top artist** card: label, artist name, round artwork (96 dp), and a small outlined "New" pill at the bottom right (only when the artist was not listened to before this month). **Tapping it opens Screen 2.**
  - **Top song** card: label, song title (max 2 lines), square artwork (96 dp, 4 dp corners), "New" pill (same rule). **Tapping it opens Screen 3.**
- A card with a 3 x 3 collage of covers (top artists and songs artwork), 6 dp gaps, square tiles, the 6th tile (row 2, column 3) is round.

### Screen 2 – Top 5 artists
- Title "Top 5 artists", month row with the subtitle "Top 5".
- Hero card for #1: round artwork 80 dp, "#1 · Top artist", name, minutes in green (24 sp), and "{plays} plays · {share}% of your listening".
- Card with ranks #2 to #5: rank number, round artwork 48 dp, name, "{min} min · {plays} plays", the share % in green on the right, and under each row a thin progress bar (4 dp) relative to the #1 artist.
- Footer card: "Together your top 5 artists made up X minutes, Y% of your listening."

### Screen 3 – Top 5 songs
- Same layout as Screen 2 with square artwork. Hero shows "{plays} plays" and "Artist · {min} minutes". List rows show "Artist · {plays} plays", minutes on the right, bars relative to the #1 song's plays. Footer: "Your top 5 songs were played N times for M minutes."

### Screen 4 – Time listened
- Total minutes card (same as home).
- 3 stat tiles: **Daily average** (min per day), **Weekly average** (min per week), **Longest day** (minutes + weekday and date).
- **Day by day** card: a bar chart with one bar per day of the month (100 dp high, 3 dp gaps, the highest day in bright green, others in the darker green), axis labels 1, 8, 15, 22, 29.
- **When you listened** card: four time blocks, each with name, range, minutes, a progress bar and "{share}% of listening · {n} min a day":
  - Night **21:00 – 03:00**
  - Morning **03:00 – 09:00**
  - Day **09:00 – 15:00**
  - Evening **15:00 – 21:00**
- **Every day** card: two columns listing each day ("Thu 1 … 45 min").

Every sub-screen has a back arrow that returns to the home screen; the system back button must do the same.

### Design tokens
Background `#121212`, cards `#1F1F1F` with 8 dp corners, progress track `#2A2A2A`, green `#1ED760`, darker green `#2F8F53`, muted text `#B3B3B3`, white text. Screen padding 20 dp horizontally, 12 dp between cards. The text sizes above are the target. Keep the app's own font if it has one.

## 3. Data and rules
- Every time a track ends, is skipped or playback stops, **save one `PlayEvent`** (track id, title, artist id, artist name, artwork url, start time in ms, milliseconds actually played with pauses excluded). Store them in a Room table.
- A **play** counts only when at least 30 seconds were played.
- Time-of-day block = the local hour the track **started**.
- Averages use the days that have passed when the month is the current month, otherwise all days of the month.
- Top artists are ranked by total minutes. Top songs are ranked by plays, ties broken by minutes.
- "New" = the artist/song has no event before the selected month.
- All numbers are computed by `computeSoundCapsule(events, month)` in `SoundCapsuleStats.kt` (code below). Use it, do not rewrite the maths.

## 4. How to integrate
1. Add the two Kotlin files below to the project (change the `package` line to my app's package).
2. Add one navigation destination "sound_capsule" that shows `SoundCapsuleHost(...)`. **Hide the floating bottom nav** while on this destination.
3. Add an entry point: a row/button "Your Sound Capsule" on the Library or profile screen.
4. Create the Room entity + DAO for `PlayEvent`, hook a listener into the player that writes events, and a ViewModel that exposes `SoundCapsuleStats` for the selected month (a `Flow` from the DAO mapped through `computeSoundCapsule`).
5. In `CapsuleArtwork`, use the image loader the app already uses (Coil or other) so real covers show. Keep the gradient as the fallback when `url` is null.
6. `java.time` needs minSdk 26 or core library desugaring; enable desugaring if minSdk is lower.
7. Until real data exists, wire the destination to `sampleSoundCapsule()` first to check the UI, then switch to real data.

